Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 09:22:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(motion): port the LeHu/Testfly MotionFly motion
 model

Replaces this module's motion model with the one from the standalone client's
MotionFly, which was described there as a "LeHu-style fly (Testfly port)" and
which the owner rates higher than the current implementation.

Motion model that came over:
  - speeds in blocks-per-second, converted per tick with / 20
  - hard horizontal ceiling of sqrt(5.99), the vanilla per-tick clamp
  - separate up/down horizontal factors, so climbing costs horizontal speed
  - glide as the no-input vertical rate (default -0.02, a slow settle)
  - input -> world transform against the packet's own yaw, then normalised to
    exactly the requested horizontal speed rather than trusting the raw input
  - anti-rubberband: a position jump beyond 4.5 blocks since the last tick is a
    server correction, so that tick is skipped instead of fought

Deliberately NOT ported, because they are separate subsystems rather than part
of MotionFly:
  - the collision guard (needs a live world block tracker; this client does not
    build one)
  - the movement-compliance governor (needs a correction feed from the other
    client's lagback module)

Kept from this client's old implementation: "Grant Fly Ability" (default off)
reproduces the ability packets the old module sent on its own, for servers where
injected motion alone is not enough. Off by default so the ported behaviour is
what ships.

onDisabled() now calls super so the toggle message and sound match every other
module (previously only enabling produced feedback).
