+ *
+ * WHAT CAME OVER (the actual motion model):
+ *   - speeds expressed in blocks-per-second and converted per tick with `/ 20`
+ *   - a hard horizontal ceiling of `sqrt(5.99)` (the vanilla per-tick clamp)
+ *   - separate up/down horizontal factors, so climbing cuts horizontal speed
+ *   - `glide` as the no-input vertical rate (default -0.02: a slow settle)
+ *   - input → world transform against the packet's own yaw, then normalise to
+ *     exactly the requested horizontal speed instead of trusting the raw input
+ *   - the anti-rubberband distance check: if the reported position jumped more
+ *     than 4.5 blocks since the last tick, the server moved us, so that tick is
+ *     skipped rather than fought
+ *
+ * WHAT DID NOT COME OVER (deliberately — they are other subsystems, not MotionFly):
+ *   - the collision guard (needs a live world block tracker, which this client
+ *     does not build)
+ *   - the movement-compliance governor (needs a correction feed from the other
+ *     client's lagback module)
+ *   If you want either, they are separate pieces of work, not part of this port.
+ *
+ * WHAT THIS FILE ADDS BACK (this client's own plumbing):
+ *   - `Grant Fly Ability` (default off) reproduces what this module used to do on
+ *     its own: while enabled, send the ability packets that let the client fly.
+ *     The ported motion model does not need it, so it is off by default; turn it
+ *     on for servers where injected motion alone is not enough.
+ */
